{"name":"Endeavour","hex":"#29598b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"endeavour","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["British standard spelling of endeavor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["British standard spelling of endeavor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endeavour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Inspector Morse","blocks":[{"text":"Detective Chief Inspector Endeavour Morse, GM, is the eponymous fictional character in the series of detective novels by British author Colin Dexter."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inspector_Morse"},{"title":"List of My Hero Academia characters","blocks":[{"text":"The My Hero Academia manga and anime series features various characters created by Kōhei Horikoshi. The series takes place in a fictional world where over 80% of the population possesses a superpower, commonly referred to as a \"Quirk\" . People's acquisition of these abilities has given rise to both professional heroes and villains."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cb/Mhacharacters.jpg/330px-Mhacharacters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_My_Hero_Academia_characters"},{"title":"Endeavour (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Endeavour is a British television detective drama series on ITV. It is a prequel to the long-running Inspector Morse series. Shaun Evans portrays the young Endeavour Morse beginning his career as a detective constable, and later as a detective sergeant, with the Oxford City Police CID. Endeavour is the third of the Inspector Morse series, following the original Inspector Morse (1987–2000) and its spin-off, Lewis (2006–2015)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7b/Endeavour_morse.jpg/330px-Endeavour_morse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endeavour_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.